{
  "version": "2026-11-06.3",
  "about": "PyLabRobot script skeletons (#99). Everything instrument-specific for lib/pylabrobot-export.js: the Python call shapes for each PyLabRobot API style (dialect), and for each handler its deck layout, labware and which head object (and its PyLabRobot class) runs which planner head. Every PyLabRobot name the skeleton calls is listed in 'api' with the file and line that defines it at 'commit'; scripts/check-pylabrobot-api.mjs re-finds each one at a commit (and --write updates the lines), and tests fail if a generated script calls a name not listed here. Resource factories come only from content/pylabrobot-labware.json at the same commit. Each handler's 'simulator' names the PyLabRobot simulation backend that lib/pylabrobot-export.js uses with {simulate: true}, and 'simulation' holds the lines a simulated script adds (tracking on, pauses and waits logged, each step reported); scripts/simulate-pylabrobot.mjs runs those scripts in CI (#103). A clean simulated run shows the deck, labware, tips and volumes fit PyLabRobot's model, not that the wet-lab method works.",
  "commit": "7779f506d12755f5f274b4c5cab4d095f4fccb62",
